 "_doc": "AL-81: rooms by what is in them (as in RimWorld) and how the village's houses are put together from them (src/sim/rooms.cpp, src/sim/structure_plan.cpp). A room is a space of built modules closed by walls and doors (a floor or footings under it), or an open one under a roof (a canopy on posts: a workshop outdoors). Its type comes from what stands in it: the rules below, highest priority first; needs = groups, each met by n (default 1) things of any of its types; enclosure closed | open | any. A room no rule fits is 'room' (closed) or 'shelter' (open). A building is a set of touching rooms; what it is for comes from its rooms (the highest purpose_rank, else priority: a farmhouse with a byre is a home). The same recognition reads every building: generated, raised by the player or by people, after every change. furnish: what the village generator puts in a room it makes (stations: must be reachable; decor: if there is room; at = back | side | middle | front). households / shared: how the generator puts a house together from rooms (at = main: the main volume; split: a second room of the ground floor behind a partition; upper: rooms of the upper storey; canopy: an open annex on posts; lean_to: a closed annex; porch: a roof before the door) and its shell (cells, storeys, walls, roof). Chances per seed; [a, b] = picked by seed.",
